1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,520
<i>You wanted the Bangladesh</i>

3
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,920
<i>petrochemical industry</i>
<i>analysis report, right?</i>

4
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,600
I'll send it over in a bit.

5
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:49,600
<i>Xiaoyezi.</i>

6
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:51,520
<i>Xiaoyezi!</i>

7
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:52,760
Here!

8
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:56,840
<i>I just… For a second there,</i>
<i>I felt like I'd traveled back in time.</i>

9
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,680
Back when I was the study committee member
calling roll, you'd always say, "Here!"

10
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,280
<i>Really loud.</i>

11
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,000
Really?

12
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:04,840
What's wrong?

13
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,000
You sound all muffled tonight.

14
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:08,680
Tell me about it.

15
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:11,000
I can't have you calling me Ikkyu-san
all this time for nothing.

16
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:12,560
Nothing much.

17
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,280
Maybe I'm just tired lately.
Got distracted.

18
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,400
I heard it.

19
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:21,160
You've been fidgeting
with your periodic table, haven't you?

20
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,680
<i>Ever since your father passed,</i>

21
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:28,840
<i>you started collecting</i>
<i>the elements on the periodic table.</i>

22
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,120
<i>You said you lost your dad,</i>

23
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:34,000
and at least collecting them all

24
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,560
would make you feel
like you owned the world.

25
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:39,760
So you only fidget
with your treasures when you're upset,

26
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,920
clinking and clanking them around
like just now.

27
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,240
<i>Come on. What happened?</i>

28
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,520
Nothing.

29
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,000
I've fallen for someone.

30
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:06,600
But?

31
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:11,080
But it was over before it even started.

32
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,120
<i>It's okay.</i>

33
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,040
<i>I've really come to terms with it.</i>

34
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:21,120
Like looking through the giant eye
of a deep-sea blue hole,

35
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:26,160
all the beauty is just an illusion.

36
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,960
What does he mean by that?

37
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,440
Do you think
he's actually working right now?

38
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:42,440
Or like me, unable to focus on anything?

39
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,200
<i>I have to do something.</i>

40
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,720
<i>Got home safe?</i>

41
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,400
<i>Yeah.</i>

42
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:16,320
XU CHI

43
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:17,519
<i>Working?</i>

44
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,720
<i>No. Just staring into space.</i>

45
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:37,680
YANG RUI

46
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,560
ANSWER

47
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,560
Hello?

48
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,680
<i>Are you asleep?</i>

49
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,760
Not yet.

50
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,440
What's up?

51
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,200
I have something to tell you.

52
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,480
Xu Chi.

53
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,840
I like you.

54
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:07,880
<i>I know you take time to warm up to people.</i>

55
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:12,240
<i>So I held back.</i>
<i>I didn't want to pressure you.</i>

56
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,360
But when you pulled
your hand away just now,

57
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,640
it really hurt.

58
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,840
I…

59
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:23,440
Tell me… Was I… Was I not good enough?

60
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:28,800
<i>So, is there nothing about me</i>
<i>that attracts you?</i>

61
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:31,120
That's not it. You're great.

62
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,520
Then can we give it a try?

63
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,920
<i>Just a try.</i>

64
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,800
<i>You can call it off anytime.</i>

65
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,200
<i>Alright?</i>

66
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,120
Please say something.

67
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,240
- Okay.
- Really?

68
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,520
Really.

69
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,200
Then tomorrow, when I hold your hand,
you can't pull away.

70
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:59,240
Uh, let's talk about tomorrow
when it comes.

71
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:02,160
I… I'm a bit confused right now.

72
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,720
Good night.

73
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,800
YE THE LEGEND SENT AN IMAGE

74
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:15,280
<i>UNLOCK THE SECRETS OF EXECUTION</i>

75
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,000
<i>This should help with</i>
<i>the implementation phase of your proposal.</i>

76
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,280
<i>Already emailed it to you.</i>

77
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,000
<i>You need to organize</i>
<i>the documents this week.</i>

78
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:25,040
<i>Make sure to confirm the timelines.</i>

79
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,640
<i>See? He's totally fine.</i>

80
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,040
<i>Stop overthinking, will you?</i>

81
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,720
<i>This is well noted.</i>

82
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,600
We have no shared interests
or common ground!

83
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,040
So let's break up, okay?

84
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,320
Did you actually like me
when we got together?

85
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,040
Am I just a replacement for someone else?

86
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,520
Say it!

87
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,600
Explain it to me! Say it!

88
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,960
I just got the official notice
from Celestial Insurance.

89
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,760
They've adopted our Plan B!

90
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,720
Maxmise's signature celebration.

91
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,680
Only happens for big wins.

92
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:06,960
Xu Chi. You deserve
the most credit for this one.

93
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:22,880
Thank you, everyone.

94
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:26,480
I… I just threw out a rough idea
to spark conversation.

95
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,200
I'm still new at this,
so I have a lot to learn

96
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,240
from all of you

97
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,520
when it comes to refining
the draft going forward.

98
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,120
No excessive modesty allowed.

99
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,960
You're an SBA now.

100
00:08:35,039 --> 00:08:36,400
No pretending to be a rookie.

101
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,000
- Ms. Xu!
- What a coincidence.

102
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,640
Heading to Celestial?

103
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,600
You and your boyfriend just got together.
Why isn't he driving you?

104
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:58,000
He's going to HQ. I'm going to the branch.
We're not going the same way.

105
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:00,560
I actually have a project over that way.

106
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,560
- I'll give you a ride.
- That'd be great.

107
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:11,760
So you admit Yang Rui is your boyfriend?

108
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,880
If you want to ask about Tianna,
just say it.

109
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,760
Stop beating around the bush.

110
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,360
Alright. Got it.

111
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:23,000
So with you, I can't be subtle.
I have to be direct, right?

112
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:27,280
I saw her staring at her desk
for a long time

113
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:29,080
after the meeting,
before she started working.

114
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,480
Did she get chewed out during the meeting?

115
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,040
No way.

116
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,360
Ma Ke is too smooth for that.

117
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,920
Whether he messed me over
or I messed him over,

118
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,200
he acts like nothing ever happened.

119
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,120
The client didn't pick Tianna's proposal.

120
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,280
Ma Ke gave her comfort and encouragement.

121
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:44,720
He just assigned her

122
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:47,200
the same amount of work
that he gave me at the meeting.

123
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:49,680
He made sure to show
his expectations and regard for her.

124
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,360
That's good.

125
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:55,280
I'm relieved.

126
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:00,000
So the rumor was true then.

127
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,520
Ma Ke did steal your proposal.

128
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:04,120
Then what are you going to do?

129
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,040
Just take it

130
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:08,040
and finish this project under him,
all nice and polite?

131
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:09,840
What else can I do?

132
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,840
You can't go through life
without taking a few hits.

133
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:19,800
I got bitten, so I showed a little fang
to make sure he doesn't try it again.

134
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,680
That's mission accomplished.

135
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,520
What?

136
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,600
Something's off.

137
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,520
You're off.

138
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:33,600
Look. If you have someone you like
and you won a project,

139
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:35,320
you should be happy.

140
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,800
You don't seem excited at all.

141
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:40,520
I am excited. Super excited.

142
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,880
Stop pretending to be a shrink.

143
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:45,160
Oh, come on. That's your idea of excited?

144
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:47,240
And I haven't even gotten
to the shrink part yet.

145
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:51,120
See, when I'm pursuing Tianna,
I'm always on edge,

146
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,160
worrying about her every second.

147
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,680
Even the tiny, trivial stuff
matters to me.

148
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,800
But you?

149
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:58,000
You're totally calm
when Yang Rui's brought up.

150
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:01,120
And I'm close with him,
but you never ask me anything.

151
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,600
You don't ask about his likes or habits.

152
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:08,560
So, there is always only one truth.

153
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:10,520
You don't like him that much.

154
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:14,320
Stop playing detective.

155
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,280
We agreed. We're just giving it a shot.

156
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:19,360
Maybe we'll grow on each other.

157
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:22,840
Love is a spark,
not something you force until it fits.

158
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:26,960
Alright, alright. Detective Zhaonan,
since you're so clear-headed,

159
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:29,520
why are you still barking
up the wrong tree with Tina?

160
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,720
What are you talking about?

161
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:35,000
She's not a wrong tree.
She's a prized orchid!

162
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,760
Say that again.
I'll record it and send it to her.

163
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,920
Sorry. I'm sorry.

164
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:42,320
Even if you defend her behind her back,
she won't be moved when she hears it.

165
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,440
It's fine. As long as you're moved.

166
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:47,440
Then you can just step up
and become the official one.

167
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,360
What?

168
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:51,560
How did I never realize
we have such great chemistry?

169
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:54,560
Look. We come from the same background.

170
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:56,120
We have the same goals.

171
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,720
We're both good-looking and capable.

172
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,320
I have a car,
and you're buying an apartment.

173
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,800
- Stop. I get it.
- In the future, we'll…

174
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:02,680
You're like a werewolf.

175
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,840
And Bu Tianna is your full moon.

176
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:05,800
The moment she's mentioned,

177
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,240
you start transforming
and talking nonsense.

178
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:12,640
I'm speechless.

179
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,320
PRIVATE, DO NOT ENTER

180
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,840
Who's there?

181
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,600
Miss.

182
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,960
Scared me.

183
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,520
What's wrong?

184
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:49,920
What happened?

185
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,080
Xiaojie's toy is in Miss Bu's room.

186
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,000
He's fussing for it.

187
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,640
I knocked.

188
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,360
I thought no one
was in the room, so I came in.

189
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,840
Let me say this again.

190
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:01,720
Even if I'm not here, you're not allowed
in my room without my permission.

191
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:04,360
Alright, alright.

192
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,960
It was a misunderstanding. Go on.

193
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:07,000
Xiaojie's waiting.

194
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:11,640
Mom.

195
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,160
We have so many rooms.

196
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,920
Why do you have to keep
his toys in my room?

197
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,200
You're hardly ever home.

198
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,320
This room gets great sunlight.

199
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:22,080
Sometimes, I have Xiaojie play in here.

200
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:25,280
He gets some sun
without getting dirty in the yard.

201
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,720
So after I get married,

202
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,000
I won't even have the right
to live in this house anymore?

203
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,000
You're overthinking again.

204
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:34,280
We're family. What's wrong
with using your room?

205
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:39,400
When you were little,
you'd go into your dad's room

206
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:41,680
and take over his desk to do homework.

207
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:42,600
Don't you remember?

208
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,680
We never got mad.

209
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:50,600
Nana, you just think too much.

210
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:54,600
I had Xiaojie
so you'd have another family member,

211
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:56,320
not another enemy.

212
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:04,200
Oh, your dad checked out a villa
in Sanya a while back.

213
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:07,760
He said there's
a round room facing the ocean.

214
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,560
You'd love it.

215
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:12,760
It's for you and your future husband.

216
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:16,800
Okay.

217
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:18,680
I get it, Mom.

218
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,280
Why are you back so late?

219
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,880
Do you want something to eat?

220
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,680
Did you tell Tianna
what I told you to say?

221
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:02,520
Yeah. It actually worked.

222
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:05,480
I'll drop another hint
tomorrow at breakfast.

223
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,520
I'll tell her I spent half the night
rubbing your back.

224
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,560
She'll feel bad for you
when she hears that.

225
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:11,960
If I keep saying it,

226
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,600
she'll surely want
to come home more often.

227
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,840
But we have to take it step by step.

228
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:21,640
We can't let Tianna
stay so hostile toward Xiaojie.

229
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,160
Then bring it up with her more often?

230
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:27,840
Tell her how many favors you called in
to help her with that insurance project.

231
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,880
She's still too naive.

232
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:31,760
Does she really think
that bringing a few gifts

233
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,160
and being polite

234
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:37,600
would make people hand over
such important internal research data?

235
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,080
That was all because of my connections.

236
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:42,440
Wait, if you helped her out,
why did you go out of your way

237
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,200
to have someone
tell Mr. Zheng at Celestial

238
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,440
to reject her proposal?

239
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:50,000
She went into consulting
without my permission.

240
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:54,320
Back when she landed the Ande Energy deal,
she was so full of herself.

241
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:58,840
If I didn't knock her down a peg
this time,

242
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,760
she'd think she's invincible.

243
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:07,120
Give her a few setbacks at work,
then shower her with warmth at home.

244
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,880
With a bit of push and pull like this,

245
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:12,360
it won't be long
before she feels burned out at Maxmise.

246
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:16,800
Then, getting her back to our company
will just fall into place.

247
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:21,040
How can you use business tactics
against your own daughter?

248
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,280
That's not fair to say.

249
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,920
I'm doing this for her own good.

250
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,440
But what about Tianna?

251
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:30,160
She's always so rebellious,
always pushing back against me.

252
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,960
Don't keep calling her Tianna.

253
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:34,440
It's Nana. It's Nana.

254
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,360
Ms. Zhu, look.

255
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:52,080
I've already divided this project
into four modules.

256
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,680
You take these four modules and…

257
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,040
- Hold on.
- Do you need a break?

258
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,120
I'm fine.

259
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:04,520
Morning. I brought you some rice balls.

260
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:06,480
Breakfast made with love?

261
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,319
Ma Ke said Celestial is having
a company-wide team-building this weekend.

262
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,079
So our team gets a half day off.

263
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:13,640
Want to think about where
we should go this weekend?

264
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:17,760
Some girl from the consulting firm
just passed out!

265
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,240
Tianna.

266
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:21,520
Wake up. Are you okay?

267
00:17:21,599 --> 00:17:23,560
- Wake up
- Should we call an ambulance?

268
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,480
- Let me help you up.
- Excuse me. Let me through.

269
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,839
I'm from Maxmise. Thanks.

270
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,839
Tianna! What happened?

271
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,680
- Help her sit up.
- Are you alright?

272
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,160
Easy, easy.

273
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,600
What happened?

274
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,920
Come on, sit down.

275
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:35,920
Nothing serious.

276
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,600
- Probably low blood sugar.
- Careful.

277
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:39,400
Do you have any white chocolate

278
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,480
- or sugary drinks here?
- I have juice.

279
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:41,400
Okay.

280
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,160
Here, have some.

281
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,920
How do you always manage
to pass out right when I happen

282
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:48,840
to have juice?

283
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,040
The Actuarial Department is brutal.

284
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:53,000
Two whole days, and you wouldn't
let her leave the conference room.

285
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:55,240
Even if she needed to verify the data,
she didn't have to push herself that hard.

286
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,240
Hey, that's not on us.

287
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,160
We told her so many times.

288
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,120
She refused to leave.

289
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,160
We brought food in
and she didn't touch it.

290
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,640
Have some more.

291
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:04,680
- Keep some chocolate
- Excuse me.

292
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:06,040
- in your bag from now on.
- Excuse me.

293
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,560
Sorry, everyone. Break it up.

294
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,800
Don't crowd around, alright?

295
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:11,960
- Thank you all.
- Feeling any better?

296
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:14,880
- Thanks.
- Thanks. Leave this to me.

297
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,720
Maybe you should take her to the hospital?

298
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,840
Okay. Let me check.

299
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,680
Tianna, are you alright?
Want to go to the hospital?

300
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:25,640
No need. I… I can still work.

301
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,040
- Don't move.
- No, no…

302
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:28,040
Don't worry about work.

303
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:29,920
Just go home and rest.

304
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:32,840
Xu Chi, you're a girl.
It's better if you take her home.

305
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,960
- Go ahead and take her back.
- I'll take her.

306
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,400
Have the chocolate first.

307
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,080
Let me get your bag.

308
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,680
No, no need.

309
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,800
Easy now.

310
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:01,800
There's no one else here.
No need to put on a brave face with me.

311
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,560
You were breaking out
in a cold sweat in the car.

312
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:07,440
Chi, are you happy seeing me like this?

313
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,720
You've never seen me
so pathetic, have you?

314
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:13,960
Missy, would you be happy
if you saw me down and out?

315
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:15,680
Maybe.

316
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,840
What's really going on with you?

317
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,480
- I am fine.
- You wouldn't

318
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:25,760
push yourself this hard just for work.

319
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,720
Is your family giving you trouble again?

320
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,560
Why put yourself through this?

321
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:33,800
It's not like you just found out
your parents favor boys over girls.

322
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,240
They don't just favor boys.

323
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,840
They team up to put me down and lie to me.

324
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:45,320
You think your proposal
was really that good?

325
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:46,400
It wasn't.

326
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:50,320
My dad had someone reach out
to Mr. Zheng at Celestial

327
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,520
to reject my proposal.

328
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,080
That's how you got the chance.

329
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,440
Why?

330
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:59,720
They want me back at Siwei Group early,

331
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:03,320
just to play second fiddle
to their precious son Bu Tianjie.

332
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:05,840
Xiaojie is still young.

333
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:08,960
He won't be able to take over
until he finishes his master's degree.

334
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:12,520
And that's at least 20 years from now.

335
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,520
I can't be everywhere at once.

336
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:19,600
I need someone I can trust
to watch over the business for Xiaojie.

337
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:26,920
I wanted to get into consulting
because it's the fastest way to grow.

338
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:31,640
If I can become a partner
at a top consulting firm by 35,

339
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:34,040
no one can question my ability
to be the successor.

340
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,280
But they won't even give me that chance.

341
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,040
They just want me
to go back to the company now.

342
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:39,960
They're gaslighting me.

343
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:42,760
They want me to be a stepping stone
for their precious son.

344
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:46,240
Very hilarious.

345
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:48,520
Let me show you.
This is what my parents say.

346
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:52,800
Give her a few setbacks at work,

347
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:56,240
then shower her with warmth at home.

348
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,000
With a bit of push and pull like this,

349
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:03,200
getting her back to our company
will just fall into place.

350
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:06,800
"Start her at the very bottom of finance.

351
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,280
She won't be able to pivot later anyway.

352
00:21:08,360 --> 00:21:10,720
At worst, we can trap her
with a General Manager title.

353
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:14,400
We can always have a CEO
and Board Chairman above that."

354
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,120
My mom is even funnier.

355
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:19,120
My brother is this young,

356
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:21,120
and my mom already has my dad
taking my brother to observe sales.

357
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:24,800
She says nothing matters more than sales.

358
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:29,240
So don't try to comfort me
with some flimsy words.

359
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:30,360
You have no idea

360
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:33,520
how painful it is to never
be the one chosen from the start.

361
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:35,920
I do.

362
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:40,280
I know what it feels like
to never be the one chosen

363
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,400
from the start.

364
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:44,680
That's why I let Ye Xinzhi go.

365
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,320
Why are you so stupid?

366
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,440
Where are you going?

367
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,160
Don't hold me back.

368
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,960
I'm going to go settle things
with that scumbag.

369
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:56,600
- You…
- He works at C&C,

370
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:58,040
- across from Maxmise, right?
- What are you going to do?

371
00:21:58,120 --> 00:21:59,880
I'm going to kill him! That scumbag.

372
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,280
This is a lawful society.

373
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,080
Listen to me. He didn't do anything to me.

374
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,600
You're so silly.

375
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:06,720
He fooled you
and you're still defending him?

376
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:09,000
I know these polished scumbags
inside and out.

377
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:09,920
Back in college,

378
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,360
two of my roommates
got wrecked by guys like him.

379
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:13,200
No initiating. No refusing.
No taking responsibility.

380
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:14,120
Sleep with you

381
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,120
- and then turn cold as ice.
- Stop, stop.

382
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:18,400
Nothing happened between us.

383
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:20,120
I just didn't want to keep

384
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:22,920
playing that ambiguous game anymore,
so I told him I had a boyfriend.

385
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:23,960
You dumped him?

386
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:31,560
I'm dizzy. I'm so dizzy.

387
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:32,600
Oh my.

388
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:34,640
Drink some more juice.

389
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:41,720
It took me a long time
to finally realize one thing.

390
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:45,200
That I like Ye Xinzhi.

391
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:50,760
I told you a long time ago.

392
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:53,920
Posers like that
are absolute pros at flirting.

393
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,360
You fall right in before you know it.
You just wouldn't listen.

394
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:59,360
What good is me nagging you
every single day?

395
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:01,320
Come on, I'm the one venting here.

396
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:03,600
Do you have to fire back
at every single thing I say?

397
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:08,400
Get this straight.
I'm the one who feels awful right now.

398
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:11,280
You're drinking my wine,
eating my chips, and lying on my couch.

399
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,680
I'm stuck on the floor.

400
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:14,440
Is it too much to ask you to listen to me?

401
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:15,360
Go on.

402
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,960
Anyway,

403
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,120
I realized I like him.

404
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:31,720
But at my current level,
I… I'm not good enough for him,

405
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:34,440
and I can't handle my own feelings.

406
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:40,160
He said he has feelings for me,
but not romantic ones.

407
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:46,200
I thought if I drew the line with him,
I could suppress my feelings.

408
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:50,200
And then I'd just be content
as an admirer.

409
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:55,080
But every time I see him with other women,

410
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:59,760
I… I can't help feeling jealous
and disappointed.

411
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,720
What did you say?

412
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,960
So he's stringing you along
while flirting with other girls

413
00:24:06,040 --> 00:24:06,880
in front of you?

414
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,680
Isn't that textbook scumbag behavior?

415
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:11,360
I can't hold back anymore.

416
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:12,920
- Where are you going?
- To beat him up.

417
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:18,360
I never knew you were such a hothead.

418
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:22,040
Because…

419
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:25,440
Because my parents are even worse.

420
00:24:26,120 --> 00:24:27,200
But I still love them.

421
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:30,920
So, I just take it out on other people.

422
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:36,280
You still have me.

423
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,480
I haven't settled the score with you yet.

424
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:46,400
Ma Ke bullied you like that
a few days ago.

425
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:47,600
Why didn't you tell me?

426
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:50,200
You came to my place and told me…

427
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:52,280
I'll hold nothing back from now on.

428
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:55,960
I'll… hold… hold nothing back from now on.

429
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:57,960
"I… I… I'm going to do
this and that to you.

430
00:24:58,040 --> 00:25:00,200
I'm declaring war on you."
Why do you flip-flop so much?

431
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:02,320
- Did I say that?
- You want it one way,

432
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:03,760
but you also want me
to tell you everything--

433
00:25:03,840 --> 00:25:05,520
Alright, alright. Come on.

434
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:06,440
Cheers.

435
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:18,480
Actually, I was pretty torn that day.

436
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:24,720
But when I saw Ye Xinzhi looking so down,
I knew he must have seen me with Yang Rui.

437
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:27,440
So, for some crazy reason,
I just said yes to Yang Rui.

438
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:28,960
But I don't regret it at all.

439
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:31,640
Because Yang Rui is honestly a great guy.

440
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:34,080
And Ye Xinzhi has so many admirers.

441
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,520
I want to be the one who moves on first.

442
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:37,840
I want to find my own happiness.

443
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:40,480
That way, he'll remember me.
He'll be shocked.

444
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:43,800
He'll realize that losing my feelings
was a huge loss!

445
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:46,160
Oh my goodness.

446
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,040
Well said!

447
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:49,000
Keep going!

448
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,320
- Ouch.
- Don't lose the momentum.

449
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,360
Bu Tianna,

450
00:26:06,840 --> 00:26:10,400
I've actually been pretty upset
these past few days.

451
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:17,320
It's this bitter, twisting pain inside.

452
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:20,600
It hurts so much I can't even sleep.

453
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:26,520
So I actually sympathize with Zhao Heng.

454
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:32,480
Because I know
he likes you the way I like Ye Xinzhi.

455
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:39,080
Maybe his reasons for getting
close to you aren't entirely pure,

456
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:42,240
but his feelings are real.

457
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:46,320
How do you know?

458
00:26:50,080 --> 00:26:52,200
Because at our core,

459
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:55,440
he and I are the same kind of person.

460
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:16,080
<i>So I actually sympathize with Zhao Heng.</i>

461
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:20,640
<i>Because I know</i>
<i>he likes you the way I like Ye Xinzhi.</i>

462
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:22,960
<i>Maybe</i>

463
00:27:23,560 --> 00:27:26,120
<i>his reasons for getting close to you</i>
<i>aren't entirely pure,</i>

464
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:28,760
but his feelings are real.

465
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:44,360
<i>What are you doing?</i>

466
00:27:44,440 --> 00:27:48,080
<i>Video calling someone</i>
<i>out of the blue is rude.</i>

467
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:50,400
Wait, just hear me out. Where are you?

468
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:51,320
Are you okay?

469
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:52,520
<i>Didn't Xu Chi tell you?</i>

470
00:27:52,600 --> 00:27:53,920
Xu Chi?

471
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,480
Xu Chi is with you?

472
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:57,640
Where are you? Put her on the phone.

473
00:27:57,720 --> 00:27:58,840
She's not here.

474
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,440
I'm at home. I'm fine.

475
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:01,640
Fine?

476
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:03,520
You're not lying to me?

477
00:28:03,600 --> 00:28:05,560
I wouldn't waste
that kind of energy on you.

478
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:09,680
That's a relief.

479
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:17,840
Are you at a construction site?

480
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:24,200
There's no elevator here.

481
00:28:24,800 --> 00:28:27,040
I ran all the way down
from the 17th floor.

482
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:31,760
No signal or power on the 17th floor?

483
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:34,640
And couldn't you catch your breath
before talking to me?

484
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:37,080
<i>You're just guilt-tripping me</i>
<i>for sympathy.</i>

485
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:38,400
Still got the energy to snap at me.

486
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:40,560
That means you're fine.

487
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:42,600
I really didn't think that far at first.

488
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:43,960
I just panicked.

489
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:45,640
I figured I'd drive over
to find you first.

490
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:47,680
<i>But I only knew</i>
<i>which building you were in.</i>

491
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:48,600
<i>I didn't know your unit number.</i>

492
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:51,000
<i>Besides, even if I went,</i>
<i>the security guard wouldn't let me in.</i>

493
00:28:51,080 --> 00:28:52,280
<i>I'm such an idiot.</i>

494
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:02,520
Hello? Why is it lagging?

495
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,440
Can you hear me?

496
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:07,040
<i>Is my signal bad? Here.</i>

497
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:09,040
Let me… Let me call you back.

498
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:11,040
I want ice cream.

499
00:29:12,720 --> 00:29:16,840
When I was little,
I loved ice cream from fast food places.

500
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:23,160
Because they had sweet ice cream
and lots of kids.

501
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:25,440
But my parents said it was junk food.

502
00:29:25,520 --> 00:29:27,640
They wouldn't let me have any.

503
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:29,080
<i>So after I started school,</i>

504
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:33,520
I went a really long time
without ice cream or fries or anything.

505
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:36,360
But the more they tried to stop me,
the more I wanted to do it.

506
00:29:36,440 --> 00:29:37,600
I'm in Unit 1902.

507
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:27,320
Hello, little Tianna.

508
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:32,320
I'm your Uncle Buka.

509
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:37,760
I'm here to bring you joy and happiness.

510
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,760
Why are you leaving?

511
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:51,240
What, Uncle Buka?

512
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:53,120
What cartoon has a character that ugly?

513
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:54,480
That's terrible!

514
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:15,840
I didn't really watch TV much anyway.

515
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:18,840
When I went to the shop
to borrow the costume,

516
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:22,680
they told me
all the ones I knew were already taken,

517
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:23,760
or I'd have to wait.

518
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:26,760
But I couldn't wait a single minute.

519
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:28,960
But that's okay.

520
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:39,080
From now on,
I'm your personal magic elf, Uncle Buka.

521
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:46,280
You did this on purpose!
You're so annoying!

522
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:48,080
You're so sneaky. You did this on purpose.

523
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:50,680
You're just trying to move me
with this cheap little thing, right?

524
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:52,960
You think I'd fall for that?

525
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:55,520
Men are all the same.

526
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:04,920
Stop hitting me.

527
00:32:06,120 --> 00:32:07,600
If you keep that up…

528
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:12,880
Uncle Buka might turn
into the Big Bad Wolf.

529
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:15,240
You wouldn't dare.

530
00:32:27,920 --> 00:32:30,080
Alright. The magic transfer is complete.

531
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:31,480
Time for good food.

532
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:05,800
From now on, Uncle Buka
will always be with you.

533
00:34:16,719 --> 00:34:18,520
You actually let him into your place?

534
00:34:20,080 --> 00:34:22,000
You actually tipped him off?

535
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:25,880
He and I aren't that close. Okay?

536
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:28,639
Well, things between him and me
aren't what you think.

537
00:34:28,719 --> 00:34:30,199
Stop making up stories.

538
00:34:31,880 --> 00:34:34,199
You let him in. You hugged, and you cried.

539
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,480
And I'm making things up?

540
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:38,960
He and I are just…

541
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:43,880
Fine. I'm all physical, no feelings.

542
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:45,760
Who do you think I am? I am Bu Tianna.

543
00:34:45,840 --> 00:34:46,679
Get it straight.

544
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:49,280
You're a total cold-hearted player.

545
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:53,400
Aren't you afraid
of falling for it one day?

546
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:56,199
Well…

547
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,840
Right back at you. You're no different.

548
00:34:57,920 --> 00:34:58,760
Let me tell you,

549
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:00,800
even though the project team
used your proposal,

550
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:02,520
you didn't really beat me.

551
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:09,880
Then I'll just wish you good health.

552
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:12,040
And I'll wish you
all the happiness in love.

553
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,400
A face-to-face showdown?

554
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:20,120
Classic top-tier consultants.

555
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:21,080
Impressive.

556
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:22,160
Don't get the wrong idea.

557
00:35:22,240 --> 00:35:24,080
Our team's fights
are always quite civilized.

558
00:35:24,160 --> 00:35:25,760
Never this explosive.

559
00:35:27,720 --> 00:35:29,960
I'm just kidding. Don't take it seriously.

560
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:40,040
When we talk to them later,
listen more and talk less.

561
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,680
Miss Xu, your package.

562
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:47,240
Your colleague asked me to bring it over.

563
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:48,200
Thanks.

564
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:50,320
Package?

565
00:36:11,560 --> 00:36:13,680
<i>Came across this old postcard by chance.</i>

566
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:16,120
<i>Returning the best times to you.</i>

567
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:17,640
<i>From Ye Xinzhi.</i>

568
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:20,760
What's wrong?

569
00:36:24,920 --> 00:36:26,040
Sorry I'm late.

570
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:27,040
Mr. Sun.

571
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:30,120
- Hello.
- Hello.

572
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:32,200
After getting the full lay of the land,
Maxmise's preliminary recommendation

573
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:34,680
is to work out
a microservices architecture plan.

574
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:35,600
Hold on.

575
00:36:35,680 --> 00:36:36,840
FRONTEND AND BACKEND ADMIN PANEL

576
00:36:36,920 --> 00:36:38,600
A microservices architecture plan?

577
00:36:40,520 --> 00:36:42,440
I told you we already have SOA.

578
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:44,800
Please take a closer look.

579
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:48,560
We modeled this after Ansheng,
the biggest insurer in the Netherlands.

580
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:49,560
Compared to SOA,

581
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,720
it's better suited for Celestial's
future development.

582
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,600
So everything I just said was for nothing?

583
00:36:53,680 --> 00:36:56,400
Or was I speaking a foreign language
that you can't even understand?

584
00:36:57,720 --> 00:36:58,720
Fine. Let me ask you.

585
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:00,280
What makes microservices better than SOA?

586
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:06,920
Microservices are essentially
a more decentralized version of SOA.

587
00:37:07,600 --> 00:37:09,400
Mr. Sun, you're absolutely right.

588
00:37:09,480 --> 00:37:11,760
But based on Maxmise's assessment,

589
00:37:11,840 --> 00:37:12,760
a more flexible microservices approach

590
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:14,880
would better support
Celestial's future growth.

591
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:16,440
This transformation has to happen,

592
00:37:16,520 --> 00:37:19,280
so please make sure to fully cooperate
with us on the redevelopment.

593
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:20,440
And this also needs

594
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:22,920
to be included in the delivery report
with an implementation timeline.

595
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:27,000
So, Mr. Sun, how about three months? Four?

596
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:30,920
Wait, Mr. Sun,
that's not what our team lead meant.

597
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:34,040
Microservices are lightweight and compact,
commonly used by internet companies.

598
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:35,840
SOA is an enterprise-level,
large-scale architecture.

599
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:37,960
That's basic knowledge.
Anyone in IT knows that.

600
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:39,160
You mentioned the Netherlands earlier.

601
00:37:39,240 --> 00:37:41,040
So tell me, how many people
does the entire Netherlands have?

602
00:37:41,120 --> 00:37:43,320
Of course, their insurance companies
can use microservices.

603
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:44,840
We have hundreds of millions of customers!

604
00:37:45,440 --> 00:37:46,440
Our SOA works perfectly fine,

605
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:48,040
and you want us
to just switch to microservices?

606
00:37:48,120 --> 00:37:49,480
And get it done in three months?

607
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:50,760
Do you have any idea
how much work that is?

608
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:52,840
You might as well tell me
to fly to the moon!

609
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:53,800
Wait, Mr. Sun.

610
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:57,640
Mr. Sun. Please don't be upset.

611
00:37:57,720 --> 00:37:58,560
- Mr. Sun.
- We can…

612
00:37:58,640 --> 00:38:00,360
We can discuss the specifics.

613
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:01,960
Miss Xu,

614
00:38:02,040 --> 00:38:03,640
I was there the day you presented
your proposal.

615
00:38:03,720 --> 00:38:05,280
Honestly, I was moved.

616
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:06,880
I thought you were someone
who gets things done.

617
00:38:07,480 --> 00:38:10,320
But after today's conversation,
a saying comes to mind.

618
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:14,240
"I thought you were impressive,
until you started talking about my field."

619
00:38:15,640 --> 00:38:18,440
Oh, and please don't come
to the IT Department anymore.

620
00:38:18,520 --> 00:38:19,760
It saves everyone's time.

621
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:35,240
Xu Chi.

622
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:36,840
Xu Chi!

623
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:40,920
Xu Chi.

624
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:42,720
Maybe it's your first time
seeing someone blow a fuse,

625
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:43,720
so you can't handle it,

626
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:45,080
but this kind of thing
happens all the time.

627
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:46,440
How could you make the decision

628
00:38:46,520 --> 00:38:48,720
to replace the entire SOA
without discussing it with me?

629
00:38:51,040 --> 00:38:52,080
I'm the team lead.

630
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,680
The plan is mine to decide.

631
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:55,040
And using precedent cases
from the reference library

632
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:56,600
is standard Maxmise practice.

633
00:38:58,240 --> 00:38:59,760
I'm not questioning you.

634
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:03,040
I just think if we'd discussed it first,
Mr. Sun wouldn't have pushed back so hard.

635
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:06,600
This time we just got unlucky.

636
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:07,880
This is the first time
I've run into someone like that.

637
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:09,400
Maxmise isn't magic.

638
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:11,560
How could we possibly know
every company's technical details?

639
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:13,520
Just showing them a tiny bit
is more than enough.

640
00:39:23,720 --> 00:39:26,040
You mentioned SOA earlier.

641
00:39:26,120 --> 00:39:27,360
You actually know about that stuff.

642
00:39:27,440 --> 00:39:29,000
I think we should revise the plan.

643
00:39:29,080 --> 00:39:31,800
At least don't make Celestial
replace their entire service architecture.

644
00:39:31,880 --> 00:39:34,360
No. You need to listen to me on this.

645
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,600
The plan is solid.

646
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:37,200
Mr. Sun just isn't ready to accept it yet.

647
00:39:37,280 --> 00:39:39,400
Give him the cold shoulder for a few days,
and he'll come around.

648
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:41,200
We've always done it this way.

649
00:39:42,360 --> 00:39:44,360
But that's not how you solve--

650
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:51,920
Hello, Ma Ke.

651
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:53,960
Yes. Yes.

652
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:56,600
I don't know why Mr. Sun
blew up like that.

653
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,920
Don't worry. I'll convince him.

654
00:40:01,640 --> 00:40:02,480
Xu Chi…

655
00:40:03,240 --> 00:40:04,120
Alright. Okay.

656
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:05,720
I'll tell her.

657
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:14,240
Ma Ke said

658
00:40:14,840 --> 00:40:17,560
Mr. Sun has been flat-out refusing
to change the IT architecture

659
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:19,080
and has such a strong reaction to you,

660
00:40:19,160 --> 00:40:20,440
so there's definitely more to this story.

661
00:40:20,520 --> 00:40:23,640
He said he'll look into it,
and we should put this on hold.

662
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:25,640
Put it on hold?

663
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:27,880
What does that mean? Is work on pause?

664
00:40:27,960 --> 00:40:29,000
What am I supposed to do then?

665
00:40:30,160 --> 00:40:32,680
How about you organize
the requirements for the sales-side app?

666
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:34,320
That's simple.

667
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:36,040
I'll gather feedback

668
00:40:36,120 --> 00:40:37,680
on the IT Department
from other departments.

669
00:40:37,760 --> 00:40:39,800
As for Mr. Sun…

670
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:44,720
I'll figure out a way
to put some pressure on him.
